  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Plume and CTD Data from the Juan de Fuca Ridge (PMEL Vents)",
  "description": "Plume studies have been conducted on the Juan de Fuca Ridge each year since the inception of the VENTS program. This includes extensive conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) mapping using both vertical casts and the \"tow-yo\" technique, light attenuation measurement, water sampling for chemical analysis using SUAVE.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Our repeated plume measurements permit the study of the long-term evolution of seafloor venting, as well as the discovery of new vents.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23568409",
